@label d1_scene
The slip at the cove, where Yusuf Reis keeps the working boat tied and the other one on
  blocks under a tarpaulin that has been there so long it has its own weather.
@show yusuf center neutral
Yusuf: Nermin's girl. Boy. Child. I never did learn which you were and it never mattered to the
  fish. Hand me that. No, the other that.
You hand him the other that. Then you hand him the letter.
He looks at the stamp, at the postmark, at the name in the corner, and he puts down the wrench
  very carefully as if it might go off.
@expr yusuf troubled
@if read.1 -> d1_seal_read
Yusuf(troubled): Sealed. Twenty-three years and sealed. She never even looked.
@jump d1_reading
@label d1_seal_read
Yusuf(sharp): This has been opened. Not by her. The paste is fresh. You read my brother's letter
  before you brought it to me.
Deniz:
  > "Yes. I wanted to know what I was carrying." {honest} -> d1_admit
  > "She had read it. I only read what she read." {first} -> d1_deflect
@label d1_admit
Yusuf: Well. That's honest, at least, and honesty's in short supply at this slip.
@set trust.yusuf +1
@jump d1_reading
@label d1_deflect
Yusuf(sharp): Don't hide behind a dead woman, child. It's bad manners and she'd have boxed your
  ears for it.
@set trust.yusuf -1
@jump d1_reading

@label d1_reading
He reads it standing, with his glasses on, and his lips move, and halfway down the second page he
  sits on the gunwale of the working boat because his legs have stopped consulting him.
Yusuf: He says there's a berth. There was a berth. In seventy-one.
Yusuf(troubled): I thought he never wrote. I told Mother he never wrote. She died in seventy-nine
  thinking her son never wrote.
@if read.1 -> d1_read_know
Yusuf: Is he alive, do you know? Kemal. Would you know a thing like that?
Deniz:
  > "I don't know. But Çeşme is two hours. You could find out." {first} -> d1_find_out
  > "Write to him. I'll take it to the boat on Thursday." {write} -> d1_write
@jump d1_after_write
@label d1_read_know
Yusuf: You read it. Then you know what he offered. Half. He offered me half, and I spent twenty
  years telling the café he'd taken the whole.
Deniz:
  > "He was asking you to come. He wasn't apologising for the boat, he was apologising for not being able to ask twice." {honest} -> d1_read_honest
  > "Write to him. I'll take it to the boat on Thursday." {write} -> d1_write
@label d1_read_honest
He looks at you for a long moment. Then he laughs, once, like a cough.
Yusuf(warm): Nineteen and reading old men's letters better than old men. All right. All right.
@set trust.yusuf +2
@set aux1 =1
@jump d1_after_write
@label d1_find_out
Yusuf: Two hours. It was two hours in seventy-one. I could have been there for supper.
@set trust.yusuf +1
@jump d1_after_write
@label d1_write
Yusuf(open): Paper. I'll need paper. I haven't written a letter since the army. Feride will have
  paper.
@set trust.yusuf +1
@flag yusuf_wrote_back
@jump d1_after_write

@label d1_after_write
@flag delivered.1
@if trust.yusuf >= 1 -> d1_resolved
Yusuf: Go on. Leave an old man with his boat. You've done what you came to do.
@jump d1_end
@label d1_resolved
@set resolve +1
Yusuf: Come back and help me with the other boat while you're here, if you've nothing better. Two
  pairs of hands and she'd float by Saturday. Then I'd have something to meet him in, if he came.
@if yusuf_wrote_back -> d1_end
Yusuf: And bring paper.
@flag yusuf_wrote_back
@label d1_end
