# ================================================================ letter 2: Feride
@scene deliver2 bg=cafe time=noon lut=warm music=cafe ambience=cafe
@set aux0 =2
@if drawer_action == 1 -> d2r_read
@jump d2_scene
@label d2r_read
@letter 2
@flag read.2
@label d2_scene
The café in the dead hour after lunch. Mira is out on a delivery. Feride is at the back table
  with the accounts and her glasses, humming under her breath without knowing she is.
@show feride center neutral
Feride: Sit. There's rice left. What's that face? You've the face Nermin had when the pension
  money was late.
You put it on the accounts book. İstanbul. 1978. Her name in a typewriter's hand.
@expr feride troubled
@if read.2 -> d2_seal_read
She does not open it for a long time. She turns it over, and looks at the postmark, and does
  arithmetic you can watch happening behind her eyes.
@jump d2_reading
@label d2_seal_read
Feride: It's been opened. You know what's in it.
Deniz:
  > "Yes. I'm sorry. I wanted to be ready, if you needed me to be." {honest} -> d2_admit
  > "Nermin opened it. I'm only the one who found it." {first} -> d2_deflect
@label d2_admit
Feride(warm): Ready. Child, nobody's ready for a sixteen-year-old letter. But I'll take the thought.
@set trust.feride +1
@jump d2_reading
@label d2_deflect
Feride(sharp): Nermin is dead and you are standing in my café with her glue on your fingers. Don't.
@set trust.feride -1
@jump d2_reading

@label d2_reading
She reads it. She reads it the way she reads the accounts, line by line, and when she gets to the
  part about the second piece she puts her hand flat on the table as if the table had moved.
Feride: Full scholarship. The residence. A stipend.
Feride(troubled): I sang that song at the audition because I'd forgotten the words to the other
  one. From memory. Without accompaniment. Because the pianist had gone to lunch.
Feride: I was twenty-six. I told my mother I'd failed. I married Mira's father in the November
  because there was nothing else on the calendar.
Deniz:
  > "You didn't fail. You were never told." {first} -> d2_not_fail
  > "Would you have gone?" {hard} -> d2_would_go
  > "Mira has a letter like this one. Right now. In her pocket." {honest} -> d2_mira

@label d2_not_fail
Feride(sharp): I know I didn't fail. I'm looking at it. What I don't know is what I'm supposed to
  do with that at fifty-two with a café and a daughter and knees.
@set trust.feride +1
@jump d2_turn

@label d2_would_go
A long silence, with the radio in it.
Feride(open): Yes. God forgive me. Yes. I'd have been on the next boat and this café would be a
  ruin and Mira wouldn't exist and I'd have gone anyway. That's the truth and I've never said it
  and I'll deny it to the imam.
@set trust.feride +2
@flag aux_flag_a
@jump d2_turn

@label d2_mira
@if mira_knows_conservatory -> d2_mira_known
Feride(sharp): What letter? What do you mean, a letter like this?
You have said more than you meant to, in the wrong order. You tell her: the conservatory, the
  audition in April, the dentist that wasn't.
@flag told_mira
@set trust.mira -1
@jump d2_turn
@label d2_mira_known
Feride(troubled): I know. She thinks I don't know. The dentist. She's never once in her life
  gone to the dentist without being dragged, and she went on her own in April and came back
  humming.
@flag told_mira
@jump d2_turn

@label d2_turn
@expr feride troubled
Feride: Here is what you're going to tell me, because you've the look. You're going to tell me
  this is about Mira and not about me.
Deniz:
  > "It's about both of you. She's waiting for you to say go." {honest} -> d2_both
  > "It's about you. You should have had this. Someone should say so." {first} -> d2_you
  > "Say nothing." {shut} -> d2_nothing

@label d2_both
Feride(open): Say go. As if it's one word.
She folds the letter and puts it in her apron, next to the pencil, and gets up, and puts the
  kettle on, and stands with her back to you for a while.
Feride(warm): I'll say it. Not today. Let me have a day of having been accepted to the
  conservatory first. I've waited sixteen years for it; I can have one day.
@set trust.feride +2
@flag feride_blessing
@jump d2_after

@label d2_you
Feride(warm): Someone just did. Thank you. It's a strange thing to be thanked for, carrying a
  grief up a hill, but thank you.
@set trust.feride +1
@if aux_flag_a -> d2_you_blessing
@jump d2_after
@label d2_you_blessing
Feride: And if I'd have gone, then I can hardly stand in a doorway and tell her not to. Can I. I
  can hear Nermin laughing from here.
@flag feride_blessing
@jump d2_after

@label d2_nothing
You say nothing. She looks at you, and you hold it, and after a moment she nods as if you had
  said something after all.
Feride: Sixteen years. Get out of my café, child, kindly, and let me cry over my accounts.
@jump d2_after

@label d2_after
@flag delivered.2
@unflag aux_flag_a
@if trust.feride >= 1 -> d2_resolved
@jump d2_end
@label d2_resolved
