# ================================================================ letter 3: Halil
@scene deliver3 bg=lighthouse time=noon lut=cold music=light ambience=wind
@set aux0 =3
@if drawer_action == 1 -> d3r_read
@jump d3_scene
@label d3r_read
@letter 3
@flag read.3
@label d3_scene
Ninety-one steps, and the wind at the top trying to take the envelope out of your hand before
  you have decided to give it. Halil is on the gallery with a rag and a tin of polish, as he is
  every day at this hour, because brass does not care who is watching.
@show halil center neutral
Halil: Post. There's no post on a Tuesday. There's no post up these stairs any day; I come down
  for it, as the directorate intends.
Halil(sharp): Directorate. That's their envelope. They don't write to me. I write to them, every
  winter, and they send a form.
He takes it. He reads the reference number before anything, as a man does who has filled in
  forms for a living, and his face does something you have not seen it do.
@if read.3 -> d3_seal_read
@jump d3_reading
@label d3_seal_read
Halil(sharp): Opened. You've read my business.
Deniz:
  > "Yes. I needed to know whether to bring it up the stairs at all." {honest} -> d3_admit
  > "Nermin read everything. I'm only finishing what she started." {first} -> d3_deflect
@label d3_admit
Halil: And you decided yes. Interesting. Most people decide no, with me.
@set trust.halil +1
@jump d3_reading
@label d3_deflect
Halil(sharp): Then finish it and go. I don't want her name up here.
@set trust.halil -1
@jump d3_reading

@label d3_reading
Halil: Kuşadası South. Three rooms. Mains. A school within two kilometres.
Halil(troubled): Selin was fourteen. She did her lessons by lamp because I wouldn't run the
  generator for homework. She did them anyway. She was going to go to the school on the mainland
  and come home at weekends, and I was going to be a keeper of a light with a town behind it.
Halil: Failing a reply. Failing a reply, understood as declined.
He puts the rag down on the rail, and then the tin, and squares them, and does not look at you.
Deniz:
  > "She did this to keep you both here. It wasn't personal." {first} -> d3_not_personal
  > "You could have asked. You could have gone down and asked if there'd been a reply." {hard} -> d3_asked
  > "Selin should know." {honest} -> d3_selin

@label d3_not_personal
Halil(sharp): It was personal to me. It was personal to a fourteen-year-old with a lamp. Don't tell
  me what it wasn't.
@jump d3_turn

@label d3_asked
A long pause. The wind. He laughs, which is a terrible sound.
Halil(open): Yes. I could have. I went down twice in December and stood at the counter and asked
  for stamps instead. Because if I didn't ask, I hadn't been refused. I've known that for five
  years and I've never had anyone say it to my face.
@set trust.halil +2
@jump d3_turn

@label d3_selin
Halil(troubled): Selin should know that her father wanted off this rock. That he'd have taken her
  light away from her to get a flat with mains. That's what she should know?
Deniz:
  > "She should know you asked for her sake. The school. You said the school." {honest} -> d3_selin_sake
  > "She should know you're human." {first} -> d3_selin_human
@label d3_selin_sake
Halil: The school. Yes. Put it that way, then, if you must put it any way.
@set trust.halil +1
@flag halil_told_selin
@jump d3_turn
@label d3_selin_human
Halil(sharp): She knows that. I've been human at her for twenty-one years. It's the rest she
  doesn't know.
@flag halil_told_selin
@jump d3_turn

@label d3_turn
@expr halil neutral
Halil: Here's what they don't know down there. The automatic programme is back. The crew comes in
  the spring. The light goes on a timer and I go on a pension and Selin goes on nothing, because
  there's no post to inherit from a timer.
Halil: Unless the keeper refuses to leave. Which he can, under the regulation; it's his house.
  Then they wait him out. I've been working out how long I can be waited out.
Deniz:
  > "Refuse. Stay. Let her be the one who takes it over when they're tired of waiting." {stay} -> d3_stay
  > "Or hand it to her now. Write to them. Say the post passes to her or it doesn't pass." {write} -> d3_hand
  > "Or go. Take Kuşadası, if it's still there. You've earned it." {leave} -> d3_go

@label d3_stay
Halil(open): Stay. The one word she had in that drawer forty years and I'm to take it from you
  free of charge.
Halil: All right. I stay. I was staying anyway. But I'll stay knowing why, which is new.
@set trust.halil +1
@flag halil_stays_keeper
@jump d3_after

@label d3_hand
Halil(troubled): They'd never. A woman, twenty-one, no training.
Halil: Nine years of keeping this light while I was asleep, drunk, or both, is what they'd call no
  training. I'll write. Nermin's counter can carry one more letter before they take the key.
@set trust.halil +2
@flag halil_stays_keeper
@jump d3_after

@label d3_go
Halil(sharp): Earned. There's a word. I'll think about it. Go down. Don't tell Selin yet; that's
  mine to do, badly, in my own time.
@set trust.halil +1
@unflag halil_told_selin
@jump d3_after

@label d3_after
@flag delivered.3
@if trust.halil >= 1 -> d3_resolved
