# ================================================================ letter 5: Cemil
@scene deliver5 bg=grocery time=noon lut=neutral music=none ambience=clock
@set aux0 =5
@if drawer_action == 1 -> d5r_read
@jump d5_scene
@label d5r_read
@letter 5
@flag read.5
@label d5_scene
The grocery with the shutters half down for the heat. Cemil is doing the ferry sums again on the
  back of a flour bag, as if the numbers might have changed since yesterday.
@show cemil center neutral
Cemil: Deniz. Tell me it's a cheque. Tell me a cousin of Nermin's died in America and left the
  island a ferry.
You put it on the flour bag. He reads the name of the company and goes very still.
@expr cemil troubled
@if read.5 -> d5_seal_read
Cemil(troubled): Ninety-two. Egeport. They came in the April, a man in a suit with a wheel,
  measured the cove. I wrote to them. I never heard. I thought they'd found a better rock.
@jump d5_reading
@label d5_seal_read
Cemil(sharp): Opened. You've read it. Then you know what you've brought me, and you brought it
  anyway, so sit down and let's both know it together.
@set trust.cemil +1
@jump d5_reading

@label d5_reading
He reads. At the launch he stops and reads the paragraph again, with his finger, and then he looks
  out through the half shutter at the cove, blue and empty and the only beach on the island where
  a child can swim without a parent on the rocks.
Cemil: Twice daily in season. For the lifetime of the hotel. Subsidised fare for residents.
Cemil(troubled): She sat on this for two years. The ferry was already going then; everyone knew.
  She sat on the one thing that would have kept a boat coming and she sat on it because it would
  have taken the cove.
Deniz:
  > "She was right. Look at what they wanted for it." {first} -> d5_right
  > "She had no business deciding that for a whole island." {hard} -> d5_no_business
  > "Is the offer still open?" {honest} -> d5_open

@label d5_right
Cemil(sharp): Right. Easy to be right from a counter with a pension. I've got to be right in front
  of a hundred and forty people with no boat.
@jump d5_turn
@label d5_no_business
Cemil: No. She didn't. And I'll say that at the next council and they'll agree with me and then
  they'll ask me what I'd have done with it, and I don't know.
@set trust.cemil +1
@jump d5_turn
@label d5_open
Cemil(open): Companies don't forget a beach. There'll be a telephone number on the second page.
  I could ring it. I could ring it today. That's the whole trouble with you bringing me this; I
  could ring it today.
@set trust.cemil +1
@jump d5_turn

@label d5_turn
@expr cemil neutral
Cemil: You're her grandchild. You're nineteen and you're leaving on Sunday whatever I do. So
  you're the only one on this island I can ask without it costing anything. Do I ring them?
Deniz:
  > "Ring them. A boat is a boat. The island can fight about the beach later." {leave} -> d5_ring
  > "Don't. A private launch for hotel guests isn't a ferry; it's a leash." {stay} -> d5_dont
  > "Put it to the island. Read it out at the café tonight. All of it, the beach clause too." {honest} -> d5_island

@label d5_ring
Cemil(troubled): A boat is a boat. God forgive me. I'll ring in the morning when the line's clear.
  Don't tell Feride; she'll have my hide for the breakfasts.
@flag cove_sold
@flag cemil_pressed
@set trust.cemil +1
@jump d5_after

@label d5_dont
Cemil(sharp): A leash. Yes. And a man on a leash still eats. I'll not ring. I'll put it in the
  drawer with the rest of her, and I'll have been as bad as she was, and at least I'll know it.
@flag cemil_refused
@set trust.cemil +1
@jump d5_after

@label d5_island
Cemil(open): Read it out. In front of Feride. In front of Halil, who swims there. In front of the
  children.
Cemil: She'd never have done that. Put a thing to the island and let it choose. All right. Tonight.
  And whatever they say, I'll ring or I won't, and it won't be on me alone, and that's worth the
  hiding I'll get.
@set trust.cemil +2
@flag cemil_pressed
@set aux3 =1
